+## Post-run addendum (2026-09-29, after the run and Codex review `verify-gpu-bundle-r1`; nothing above is changed)
+
+- **Executed value-loss coefficient.** Checks 3 and 4 declare 0.5·MSE for the value term (check 4's method above). As executed, `c3_smoke.py` and `c4_timing.py` compute `v_loss = 0.5·mean((v − ret)²)` (half-MSE) and add `0.5 · v_loss`, so the value term was **0.25·MSE** in both. Check 3's pass criteria (finite loss and gradients) do not depend on the coefficient. Check 4's component timings remain usable: a scalar coefficient on one loss term changes no kernel, shape or step count. The workload descriptions in `results.md` and the evidence README now state 0.25·MSE.
+- **Outer-timeout cleanup.** The executed driver started every stage in its own session and had no signal handler, so the `timeout -k 20 3540` backstop could not have terminated running stages. Both attempts ran that driver, and neither overran. The driver and launcher were revised afterwards and tested locally only (evidence README, "Post-run corrections").
cookbook/log.md:13:The [[references/failed-training-reports-status-before-distributed-cleanup|failure-reporting Reference]] and its index line still said Claude's cross-review was pending and Rust parity was blocked (148 passed, 7 failed). Both contradicted the Task 0.3 receipt (`ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/0.3-results.md`, "Claude review") and the earlier log entry: the review found no blocker, and with the git-ignored Orbit fixtures copied in, `cargo test` gave 155 passed, 2 ignored. The [[index|root index]] no longer says every Reference describes `kg/reference-2026-09-29`; the References index states each note's scope. Moving current-tree notes out of that index's "Reference branch" section is left until the in-flight lanes land.
